Now write the outputs. Verdict: APPROVE (no blocking findings; 1 important, 2 suggestions).

The machine protocol: APPROVE with remaining ⚠️/💡 findings is the expected terminal state. issueCounts must be accurate: blocking 0, important 1, suggestions 2.

Comment 1 (IMPORTANT) — isIssueOpen fail-open on transient errors:

The code at line 135: `if (!res || res.message) return false;` — any error body (rate limit, 5xx, network error body) is treated as "issue absent", routing a labeled PR with a genuinely OPEN linked issue down the orphan-carrier path: it merges immediately (fine if clean) but skips the issue-side bookkeeping — the issue keeps `pr_approved` forever and every future sweep logs "no linked open PR" for it (the PR is closed by then). Recommend distinguishing 404 from other messages: only treat Not Found/404 as absent; count other error bodies as item failure (failed++ → aggregate throw) or as a plain skip without merging.

Suggested fix sketch:

```js
function isIssueOpen(owner, name, n) {
    var res;
    try {
        res = parseMcp(github_get_issue({
            workspace: owner, repository: name, number: n
        }));
    } catch (e) {
        return false; // throwing bridges (mocks, some forges) — 404 throws
    }
    if (!res) return false;
    if (res.message) {
        var m = String(res.message).toLowerCase();
        if (m.indexOf('not found') !== -1 || res.status === '404' || res.status === 404) return false;
        throw new Error('github_get_issue #' + n + ': ' + res.message); // transient → item failure, not "absent"
    }
    return String(res.state || '').toUpperCase() === 'OPEN';
}
```

Wait — but throws inside map-back are caught per-item and treated as orphan too (`catch (e) { ... orphanPrs.push(prn) }`). Hmm! Look at the map-back loop:

```js
try {
    var n = extractLinkedIssueNumber(pr);
    if (n !== null && isIssueOpen(owner, name, n)) { ... } else { orphanPrs.push(prn); }
} catch (e) {
    say('⚠️ map-back failed for PR #' + prn + ' (treated as orphan): ...');
    orphanPrs.push(prn);
}
```

So even if isIssueOpen throws on a transient error, the catch ALSO routes to the carrier path. So my suggested fix needs the map-back catch to distinguish too — or the failure should skip the PR this sweep (leave it labeled; next sweep retries) rather than merging it now. Better recommendation: on transient failure, DON'T process the PR this sweep — skip it (it stays labeled, the next cron run retries). Only a verified-absent/closed issue takes the carrier path.

I'll write the comment recommending: 404-ish → carrier path (current behavior, correct); anything else (throw or error body) → log + skip the PR this sweep (do not merge, do not route to carrier), so a transient API hiccup never merges a PR while skipping its issue bookkeeping.

Note the test at 'orphan carrier: linked issue ABSENT (404 body, no throw)' stays green with this.

