So even if isIssueOpen throws on a transient error, the catch ALSO routes to the carrier path. So my suggested fix needs the map-back catch to distinguish too — or the failure should skip the PR this sweep (leave it labeled; next sweep retries) rather than merging it now. Better recommendation: on transient failure, DON'T process the PR this sweep — skip it (it stays labeled, the next cron run retries). Only a verified-absent/closed issue takes the carrier path.

